The most interesting of these are **BSI** and **3D stack**.

The traditional CIS is "FSI" -- light is needed to reach the light zone through the metal sheet. BSI turns the chip over, directs the light into the light zone, and quantum efficiency is significantly increased. 3D stacks are made to create a symmetry of the light layer and the logic layer to create a higher performance.

** These two technologies are high-end CIS "hard threshold"**. Sony has been used on a large scale at the consumer level, but at the industrial/science level, long-light cylindris are one of the few that can do it. The BSI process was used for multiple products in the GSENSE series, as illustrated by the new GLR 1002BSI-S name in 2026.

